,-2,1,"I presume we want the shadow overlay to be higher in the paint z-order and not take any input events (the later part is already handled in this CL)? Because we may need to round out the corners and…"],["86b73175_f238e211",100,-2,1,"I think this should be using browser view y instead of the overlay."],["aee79c3d_3c2f59af",100,-2,1,"Given we don't support the toolbar height side panel in the old layout, we can just skip setting bounds for the shadow view if we set the visibilility to false by default."],["ca0b53be_c440c96f",65,-2,1,"Could we store the insertion index (similar to tab_strip_region_insertion_index_) during add and use it instead of taking a dependency with another part of the code which is harder to maintain."],["cf828395_fa6808de",65,-1,1,"nit: looks like there is an extra semicolon here."],["e11a4f01_32bc0f8d",65,-1,1,"I would presume window scrim, find bar host should have a higher z-order than the shadow overlay?"],["ead7f052_7b93d2b2",78,-1,1,"We need to update this to reflect the current layout i.e. removing main container as a parent container."],["1d1f36ad_4177aad2",100,0,0,"Should this add browser_view_->y() to it?"]],0,1469],[7128459,20399,197,4.21,3.407,[[1,942]],[["0eef0239_ccd8cf4d",17,0,1,"nit: format this to wrap around"],["913c9097_7aa66e5a",103,0,1,"minor nit: ContentsArea seems better naming than ContentsPane."]],0,1470],[7133758,20402,95,2.361,1.866,[[1,1.0,943,97]],[["4ebe4c17_0f977fcb",103,-3,0,"Is my line of thinking here right? Instead of expanding the browser width we are shrinking the toolbar panel width to fit within the available bounds excluding the main area?"]],0,1471],[7138278,20402,32,1.341,1.058,[[1,944]],[["179e0ea3_a1d4db8c",113,0,0,"Does this value need to change? Can it stay at 50? Or is it clashing with the minimum content width?"]],0,1472],[7139018,20402,37,1.341,1.058,[[1,945]],[],0,1473],[7139678,20403,233,4.21,3.407,[[1,1.0,946,239]],[["3605d108_f92ab7e6",112,-1,1,"super nit: Let's add a brief comment explaining the purpose of this constant 👍"],["69d5524b_681ae0ef",112,-1,1,"super nit: Add a brief comment as to why we are performing the clip paths in the first place 👍"],["80ab2b9d_6544bd63",112,-1,0,"Looks like this is a generalized implementation of chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/contents_rounded_corner.h. Would it make sense to perhaps generalize that into a single implementation which we reuse?…"]],0,1474],[7147463,20405,46,1.22,0.938,[[0,189]],[],0,1475],[7148063,20405,201,4.21,3.407,[[1,1.0,947,203]],[],0,1476],[7148064,20405,160,4.21,3.407,[[1,1.0,948,162]],[["81ae2f46_76a19fea",103,0,0,"optional: Should the visibility of the webui tab strip also depend on `tab_strip_type` like in the other cases below? Even if the height is set to 0? Might not be needed but stays consistent with the…"],["b5231bee_6339f25c",103,0,0,"optional: same visibility comment as above 👍"]],0,1477],[7148678,20405,37,1.341,1.058,[[1,949]],[],0,1478],[7153658,20406,68,2.361,1.866,[[1,950]],[["71e55e30_45a4f397",103,0,0,"Question: Do we need really need to support loading bar in the new layout. Ideally with the deprecation of WebUI tab strip happening sooner than later could we get by without it? Would prefer not…"]],0,1479],[7153659,20410,51,1.341,1.058,[[1,951]],[["6b502408_96b2040a",103,0,1,"I am trying to recollect if this code around dialog positioning is still relevant anymore. Steven refactored tab dialog host and moved them to contents container. I don't know if this is still needed…"]],0,1480],[7170761,20412,109,1.661,1.339,[[33,1.0,134,107]],[],0,1481],[7170089,20412,908,10.971,8.929,[[1,952]],[["1a9ddd50_352e2734",114,0,0,"Dana, one last feedback on this. Given we browser_view_app_layout_impl.cc, wouldn't it be more clearer to have browser_view_tabbed_layout_impl.cc and browser_view_app_layout_impl.cc as specific…"],["472b48fe_880ce296",115,0,1,"Duplicate?"],["9de507e2_94e02c70",115,0,0,"Should the WebContents be added here as well? Or is that browser type specific?"],["a266f4aa_7f9a1bff",114,0,1,"Could we make these as members on BrowserLayoutParams instead of static functions? Would make it easier to call e.g. params.InsetHorizontal(amount, leading); or params.SetTop(top);"],["b5a7f647_599c6dbb",103,0,0,"I think if we are splitting out the layouts, there isn't a case in tabbed browser where there isn't a top separator. So pretty sure we can remove this."],["f927eec0_965b03c0",114,0,1,"Why is this in common vs. in impl since this is applicable only for tabbed browser?"],["fefd3e96_25d08c7c",115,0,1,"I see the thinking behind having the following funtions below in common to share as much code as possible. However, its kind of messy for having part of the implementations scattered around making it…"]],0,1482],[7170758,20412,451,7.601,6.192,[[1,0.953,953,433],[11,0.041,63,16],[19,0.006,87,2]],[["0c530e1e_133d8d49",116,0,1,"Dana, I fixed this issue on another CL: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/7155726"],["11b13dbf_ab3173c4",116,0,1,"overlay is a bit ambigous. Could name it something like overlay_controls_enabled."],["30a3a6af_deb535ac",116,0,0,"optional: `CHECK(!(tabstrip_enabled && overlay_controls_enabled));` Purely preference though."],["854be9e5_6ca4fb7d",104,0,1,"Question: Why is is_type_app check not sufficient here?"]],0,1483],[7179802,20413,77,2.361,1.866,[[1,954]],[],0,1484],[7188083,20413,1,0.143,0.09,[[1,955]],[],0,1485],[7185001,20413,36,1.341,1.058,[[1,956]],[],0,1486],[7188103,20413,8,0.421,0.3,[[1,957]],[],0,1487],[7180963,20413,56,1.341,1.058,[[1,1.0,958,1438]],[],0,1488],[7180964,20413,101,2.361,1.866,[[1,1.0,959,939]],[],0,1489],[7186239,20414,29,0.737,0.556,[[1,960]],[],0,1490],[7186823,20416,4,0.259,0.185,[[1,961]],[],0,1491],[7185002,20416,2,0.143,0.09,[[1,962]],[],0,1492],[7205081,20417,41,1.341,1.058,[[1,963]],[["2e522d68_c009ba23",117,0,0,"Trying to understand this more. It was my understanding that webui_tab_strip is initialized and destroyed based on the WebUITabStripContainerView::UseTouchabl